1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
I have a name for what happens to me.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Revival.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
When it happens, I go back in time anywhere from one to five minutes.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
And it always happens before something bad goes down.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
I've managed to stop a lot of tragedies, so far.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Hey there, Satoru.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Hey, Mom.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Are you Satoru, Fujinuma?

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
You're gonna have to come down to the station.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Hmm.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:42,980
Thank you.

12
00:01:43,000 --> 00:02:12,980
Thank you.

13
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,120
See Maskman? Next week's the last episode.

14
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:19,500
I totally forgot to watch Black.

15
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:26,000
1988. February 15th?

16
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:29,420
Good morning, everyone.

17
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:36,660
Well, Satoru, you're gonna take your seat?

18
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:39,700
Huh? Oh. Yes, sir.

19
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:41,920
Where was my seat again?

20
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:49,260
You still asleep or something?

21
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:51,840
That's Kaio's desk, you doofus.

22
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:53,120
Oh, yeah.

23
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:54,040
No Kaio.

24
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:56,760
I'll have to mark her tardy again.

25
00:02:56,760 --> 00:03:02,640
Satoru, are you, like, in love with Kaio?

26
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:06,840
You'd make a cute couple. You're both weird.

27
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:09,260
Here we go, folks.

28
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,600
Is this for real?

29
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:15,400
Why did I get dropped back to this time?

30
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,220
What's going on?

31
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,960
This is 18 years ago.

32
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:31,600
How far did you get on Dragon Quest 3?

33
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:32,860
Level 15.

34
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:33,840
That's it?

35
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,100
Nah, just testing.

36
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,000
I'm on 25.

37
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:37,320
You liar!

38
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:42,620
Hey, what's wrong?

39
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:45,860
Um, my head hurts, so I'm gonna see the nurse.

40
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,320
Then why are you taking your bag?

41
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:51,640
Don't worry about it.

42
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,900
I'll let the teacher know where you went.

43
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,260
What the hell's going on?

44
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:58,880
Is this revival?

45
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:01,780
I don't get it.

46
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:03,720
Why'd I go back this far?

47
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:12,400
Mom!

48
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:12,460
Mom!

49
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:12,500
Mom!

50
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:39,820
Hello.

51
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:41,080
Sorry to keep you waiting.

52
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:46,980
It's one of the neighbors.

53
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,320
That's right.

54
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:55,560
She'd be at work now.

55
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:59,800
Mom!

56
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:22,940
Mom!

57
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:39,560
Hey there, kiddo.

58
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,360
Mom.

59
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:45,780
What's wrong?

60
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:48,860
Nothing. Just happy to see you.

61
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,500
You little weirdo.

62
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:51,900
So what do you want for dinner?

63
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:53,120
Hamburger or meatballs?

64
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:55,820
Uh, hamburger?

65
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,460
You getting hungry or what?

66
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:23,420
You're in a good mood.

67
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:26,200
Not like this morning when you pitched your little fit.

68
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,360
Guess you found your recorder, huh?

69
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:30,220
Yeah, I did.

70
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:31,820
I'm sorry.

71
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:35,100
It's nothing to cry about, kiddo.

72
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:44,960
I remember moments like this.

73
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:49,940
I guess back then I didn't realize how important they'd be.

74
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,520
I let times like this slip by without even thinking about them.

75
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:59,400
This is revival.

76
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:03,620
It's another chance.

77
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:08,640
And there's no way I'll let this one slip by.

78
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:11,580
Mom.

79
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:13,180
Hmm?

80
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,660
It's really good.

81
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:15,800
Thank you.

82
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:17,800
Are you sure you're okay?

83
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:18,800
Thanks for dinner.

84
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,280
You're welcome.

85
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:27,820
Am I supposed to do the next 18 years over again?

86
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:29,480
Morning, Satoru!

87
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:30,620
Hey, Asamu.

88
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:31,160
Morning.

89
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:35,040
If this is revival, then I'm here for one reason.

90
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,800
To stop something bad from happening.

91
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:42,300
Maybe to save my mom, I have to start here.

92
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:45,840
But why so far back?

93
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:47,700
Nothing seems off here.

94
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,840
That's Kaya Hinazuki.

95
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:05,540
She lived alone with her mom, too.

96
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,840
And bam.

97
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:08,340
Whoa!

98
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:16,400
How'd she get that?

99
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:20,680
You know what I think sucks about this group?

100
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,760
There's no one to talk Dragon Quest with.

101
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:23,020
Huh?

102
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:24,300
Uh...

103
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:27,760
I mean, Hiro's a Final Fantasy fan, and Kazu only plays shooters.

104
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:29,200
That's Hiro.

105
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:30,560
And Kazu.

106
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,020
I remember them.

107
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:34,680
Heck, Satoru doesn't even have a Famicom.

108
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:36,560
No, I didn't.

109
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:37,780
Jeez, Asamu.

110
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:41,260
Oh, if we all played Dragon Quest, then that's all we'd ever talk about.

111
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:45,540
The cool thing about our group is, we all like different things, so it's never boring.

112
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:46,660
That's Kenya.

113
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:49,060
Out of all of us, he was the brainiest.

114
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,380
Can I ask you something, Satoru?

115
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,740
It's kinda personal.

116
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:54,460
Sure.

117
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:55,440
Go ahead.

118
00:08:55,780 --> 00:08:56,260
Do you...

119
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:58,080
have a crush on Kayo?

120
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:58,620
Huh?

121
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:00,500
I saw you staring at her.

122
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:01,880
No way, really?

123
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:03,220
He totally was.

124
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:05,040
This morning, he just stood there staring.

125
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:06,540
He couldn't take his eyes off her.

126
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:07,600
Dang it, Satoru!

127
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,600
If you're in love with her, you should've come to me for advice.

128
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,600
Romance is right up my alley.

129
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,000
But...

130
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,580
No buts about it.

131
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:16,600
I'll fix it so you can hook up with Kayo.

132
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,800
Could you keep your voice down?

133
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:19,180
Why?

134
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:21,600
Well, it's like...

135
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,280
I don't love her.

136
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:25,100
Just curious about her.

137
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:26,360
That's the same thing!

138
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,720
You're brave to admit it!

139
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,140
Don't you worry about a thing!

140
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:32,000
By the end of the day, you'll be talking with your dream girl!

141
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:32,340
Ha!

142
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:32,520
Ah!

143
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,400
You're an idiot.

144
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:37,440
Damn, she's cold.

145
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,680
That's how you say hello?

146
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:42,340
I said that out loud.

147
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,280
Oh, crap.

148
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:47,340
I bet Kazu straight up told her I had a crush on her.

149
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,680
Um, Kayo?

150
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:56,780
I was thinking, since we walk home the same way, maybe we could be friends?

151
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:58,000
Friends?

152
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:00,320
What is it you like about me?

153
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,840
She's a pain in the ass.

154
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,860
You don't have to answer that if you don't want to.

155
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:07,460
I think I know.

156
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,240
You're just like I am.

157
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,300
You're fake, too.

158
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,320
Wait...

159
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,200
Does she know about me?

160
00:10:17,060 --> 00:10:18,900
I saw you running home yesterday.

161
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:19,780
Huh?

162
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:21,260
You looked happy.

163
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,440
Do you love your mom that much?

164
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:26,180
Yeah.

165
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:28,660
That's good.

166
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:30,740
Wait.

167
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:31,420
Kayo!

168
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:32,800
Hold up!

169
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,560
So how about it?

170
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:35,900
You want to be friends?

171
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:38,400
Are you serious?

172
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:40,900
So, like...

173
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:43,800
Does that mean you'd kill to protect me?

174
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:46,260
No, you don't get it!

175
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:47,280
I could have saved her!

176
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:52,700
Something bad was happening to Kayo in the days before she died.

177
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:57,600
Maybe if I can stop it, I can save her.

178
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:10,900
I think I know.

179
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,680
You're just like I am.

180
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:13,720
You're fake, too.

181
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:16,800
I doubt she could tell I wasn't really a kid.

182
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:20,480
I guess maybe I might have been acting a little weird,

183
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:23,320
but that's pretty much how I was back in those days.

184
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:25,680
I wanted friends,

185
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:28,800
so I tried acting like the person I wanted to be.

186
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:31,500
If you have courage, you can do anything.

187
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:39,140
It was the only way I knew how to fit in in my middle school world.

188
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:39,860
No.

189
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:42,100
We were going to send a search party in the house.

190
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:43,620
I bet she saw through that.

191
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,860
But she said I was like her,

192
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:48,480
so maybe she's hiding her true self, too.

193
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:52,280
So, how'd you make out?

194
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:53,700
Yeah, man.

195
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:55,280
You gonna tell us how it went or what?

196
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,740
Did you guys walk home together?

197
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:57,660
Did you hold hands?

198
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:58,520
Geez, no.

199
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:00,860
We just talked for a little bit, that's all.

200
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:01,600
Just you two?

201
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:02,300
Alone?

202
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:03,180
Mm-hmm.

203
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:04,240
Sweet!

204
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:05,920
That means she totally likes you!

205
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:06,720
Dude, seriously.

206
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:08,440
She never talks to anyone alone!

207
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:09,600
You want me to give her another...

208
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:12,420
Could they be more annoying?

209
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:14,140
Take it easy, guys.

210
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:16,760
Pressuring him like this isn't gonna help him.

211
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:18,320
You're right.

212
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:21,600
He's talking about something else, but...

213
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:21,920
Yeah.

214
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:22,980
Satoru.

215
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:26,280
In sixth grade, we'll all be in the same class again.

216
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:27,600
So there's no rush.

217
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:28,300
Right.

218
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:31,100
Attention, students.

219
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,800
When did Kyo disappear again?

220
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:36,020
Ugh, I'm running out of time.

221
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,080
Satoru, come on!

222
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:38,460
Yeah, come in!

223
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:41,720
It's cold.

224
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,520
By the way, where are those kick-ass McGregor gloves you got?

225
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:45,520
Oh, yeah.

226
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,860
I remember I had a pair of those.

227
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:49,600
I guess maybe I left him somewhere.

228
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:52,600
Oh, well, they're probably at the hideout then.

229
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:54,280
Hey, guys.

230
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:56,000
Can we go to the hideout today?

231
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,680
What are you talking about?

232
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:58,160
Remember?

233
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:00,460
We said we wouldn't go there if it snows,

234
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:01,960
because everyone would see our tracks.

235
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:03,700
Oh, we did?

236
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:04,960
Oh, right.

237
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:05,500
Yeah.

238
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:07,140
See you tomorrow.

239
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:07,860
Later, dudes.

240
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:08,160
Later.

241
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:08,460
Bye.

242
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:09,760
See ya.

243
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:13,320
Kenya!

244
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:15,820
Thanks for speaking up.

245
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:18,800
It's like they were making such a big deal out of it,

246
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:19,740
I was freaking out.

247
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:20,980
Yeah, I bet you were.

248
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,600
You don't have to thank me, though.

249
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:25,660
By the way, about Kyo.

250
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:28,840
I think it's great you want to get closer to her and all,

251
00:13:29,340 --> 00:13:31,540
but I get the feeling there's something else going on.

252
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:34,420
I don't mean to be nosy or anything,

253
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:37,420
but I'm here if you need to talk to someone.

254
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,240
And not just me.

255
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:40,480
The other guys are, too.

256
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:42,000
Thanks.

257
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:43,020
And yeah,

258
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:45,700
I know everyone's just trying to help.

259
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:48,700
Kazuh did get Kyo to talk to me after all.

260
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:51,620
So, want to talk about it?

261
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:52,760
About what?

262
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:53,580
About Kyo.

263
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,160
Oh, right.

264
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:56,760
Did you talk to her?

265
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:58,940
Yeah, only for a bit.

266
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:01,100
She even opened up a little by the end.

267
00:14:01,620 --> 00:14:02,220
That's good.

268
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,140
I know you got a lot on your mind,

269
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:05,300
but I was wondering.

270
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:09,320
You read the essays yet?

271
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:10,400
Huh?

272
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,480
No, I haven't.

273
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:14,580
There are a couple of interesting ones.

274
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:15,800
You should check them out.

275
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,280
I better go.

276
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:18,140
See you tomorrow.

277
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:19,320
See ya.

278
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:29,080
I bet Kenya was hinting at Kyo's essay being the interesting one in this.

279
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:34,800
The Town Without Me by Kyo Hinazuki.

280
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,900
When I get bigger,

281
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:39,220
big enough to go somewhere by myself,

282
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:42,200
I want to go someplace far away from here.

283
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:44,760
I want to go to an island.

284
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,180
An island without any people.

285
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:51,980
An island that doesn't have any pain or sadness on it either.

286
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:57,180
There are no grown-ups, kids, classmates, or teachers.

287
00:14:58,060 --> 00:14:59,460
Even my mom's not there.

288
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,580
When I feel like I want to climb a tree,

289
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,160
I can climb it.

290
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:06,700
I'll go for a swim if I want to.

291
00:15:07,260 --> 00:15:08,700
And sleep when I want to.

292
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,720
On the island,

293
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:14,200
I'll think about what's going on in the town without me.

294
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:17,520
Kids go to school like nothing's changed.

295
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:20,700
Grown-ups go to work like nothing's changed.

296
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:24,320
Mom eats her dinner like nothing's changed.

297
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:27,500
And when I think about the town without me,

298
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:30,040
I feel relief more than anything.

299
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:34,600
All I want is to go far away.

300
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:37,820
Her essay's a cry for help.

301
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:39,260
No doubt about it.

302
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:41,160
I'm home!

303
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:43,560
Thanks for dinner.

304
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:47,420
Kenya probably thought I was interested in her

305
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:48,480
because of the essay.

306
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,060
After reading it,

307
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,220
now I'm even more worried about her.

308
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:53,660
Hey, Mom?

309
00:15:53,940 --> 00:15:54,580
Yeah, what's up?

310
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:55,840
For my birthday,

311
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,620
can I invite some friends over?

312
00:15:58,220 --> 00:15:59,080
Mm-hmm.

313
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:01,800
Sure, but our place is kind of small.

314
00:16:01,980 --> 00:16:03,080
How many friends are we talking?

315
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:03,940
Not too many.

316
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:04,840
Just five.

317
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:06,180
You know,

318
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:08,400
this is the first time you asked to have a party.

319
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:09,900
Should I get a big cake?

320
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:10,480
Yeah.

321
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:11,620
Thanks, Mom.

322
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:13,780
I know what I have to do now.

323
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:16,600
I have to get to know Kaio even better.

324
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:20,560
I'm gonna do what I didn't the first time.

325
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:23,740
If I can make her do something different now,

326
00:16:24,260 --> 00:16:26,440
maybe it'll be enough to change her fate.

327
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,340
Maybe it'll change everything.

328
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:33,940
Hey, you still awake?

329
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:35,880
You said five.

330
00:16:36,180 --> 00:16:37,480
Did you get yourself a girlfriend?

331
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:40,040
Alright.

332
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:41,440
Goodnight, kiddo.

333
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:42,560
Witch.

334
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:45,460
I just remembered something.

335
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:48,440
I didn't show my mom my essay back then

336
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,060
because I knew she'd read it

337
00:16:50,060 --> 00:16:51,640
and see it right into my soul.

338
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:54,400
What did I write about again?

339
00:16:58,860 --> 00:17:00,880
I'll go on home with great dragon quest.

340
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:01,540
Me too.

341
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,360
Man, it's snowing again.

342
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:04,660
No hideout today.

343
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:04,940
Huh?

344
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:06,220
Satoru!

345
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:07,240
Kaio's leaving.

346
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:08,360
Don't you want to talk to her?

347
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:09,340
Osamu.

348
00:17:09,540 --> 00:17:10,420
It's okay, Kenya.

349
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:11,560
It's no big deal.

350
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:12,880
And thanks, Osamu.

351
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:13,920
See ya.

352
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:15,160
See ya.

353
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:15,720
Later, dude.

354
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:18,980
Can you believe how brave he's gotten?

355
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:23,520
I didn't have to run.

356
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:25,580
I already knew where I'd find Kaio.

357
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:29,120
I was pretty sure her mom was hitting her

358
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:30,200
and if that was true,

359
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:32,060
she wouldn't be going home right away.

360
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,180
She'd go hang out at the park

361
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:35,780
until it got darker out.

362
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:38,520
Before, I just thought she was weird.

363
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:40,220
Not anymore.

364
00:17:40,220 --> 00:17:40,420
Not anymore.

365
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:40,480
Not anymore.

366
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,840
Kaio!

367
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:52,940
Satoru, what do you think you're doing out here?

368
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:55,240
I was gonna say the same thing.

369
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:56,820
I meant what I said.

370
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,160
I want to be friends.

371
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,120
I won't kill anyone.

372
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:02,420
That's too much.

373
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:03,260
No, duh.

374
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,300
That was a joke.

375
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:06,600
I hate dealing with her type.

376
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,200
You know what you're doing, Satoru.

377
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,020
You're just pretending.

378
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:13,220
Pretending to smile

379
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:14,500
and being nice

380
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:16,240
and worrying about people.

381
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,860
But I don't think it's bad or anything.

382
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,900
I can't tell what you're really like.

383
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:24,380
That sounds funny coming from me.

384
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:28,920
Everything you said's true.

385
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:30,380
I am pretending.

386
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:33,100
I want people to like me.

387
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:34,420
I want to have friends.

388
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:36,080
So I asked myself,

389
00:18:36,420 --> 00:18:38,540
what can a loser like me do to have that?

390
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:41,820
And you know what?

391
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:44,340
I tried liking everyone and it worked.

392
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:46,100
It was hard at first,

393
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:47,080
but after a while,

394
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:48,020
it got easier.

395
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:52,160
Yeah.

396
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:53,640
And like,

397
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:55,080
the more you do it,

398
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,720
the better the chance it comes true.

399
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:59,260
The more I talk about it,

400
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:01,080
the better the chance it'll come true.

401
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:04,200
It's like deja vu all over again.

402
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:07,200
To get what you want,

403
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:08,440
you have to make an effort.

404
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:10,400
You have to try new things

405
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,960
and keep inspiring yourself.

406
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:13,600
That's how you change.

407
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:16,260
Is that what Kaio's doing too?

408
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:18,820
I can tell she's suffering now.

409
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,680
But unlike me,

410
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,220
she acts like she doesn't care.

411
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:25,040
Pretending like she can't feel anything at all.

412
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,900
But she's only ten.

413
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:28,380
She's not strong enough

414
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:30,000
to change her situation at home.

415
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:31,840
Hey Kaio,

416
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:33,520
I brought something for you.

417
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:34,620
What?

418
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:37,280
I'm having a birthday party

419
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:38,260
and I want you to come.

420
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,320
Are you sure it's okay?

421
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:42,440
I mean,

422
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,960
won't there be tons of people?

423
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,240
Oh, I don't know yet.

424
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:46,780
But I wanted to give you

425
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:47,800
the first invitation.

426
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:51,720
It's on March the 2nd.

427
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:52,460
Huh?

428
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:55,220
You're gonna come, right?

429
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:57,760
Uh-huh.

430
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:00,420
Hey,

431
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:02,340
aren't your hands cold?

432
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:03,000
Huh?

433
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:04,440
Oh, yeah.

434
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,280
They kinda are.

435
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:06,840
I had some new gloves,

436
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:07,940
but I think I lost them.

437
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:16,620
Take it easy, dude.

438
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:17,860
You're 29.

439
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:20,440
Why are you getting all flustered?

440
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:22,380
Satoru,

441
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:23,300
are you okay?

442
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:24,800
Uh-huh.

443
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:25,580
I mean,

444
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:27,140
my hands way bigger than yours, huh?

445
00:20:27,340 --> 00:20:28,080
You're an idiot.

446
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:30,880
Even so,

447
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:33,600
you seem like you're okay.

448
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:35,400
It's easy talking to you.

449
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,540
Well,

450
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,380
it's cause I decided

451
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:40,440
to be honest with you.

452
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:43,080
I said that out loud.

453
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:46,880
Wait,

454
00:20:47,060 --> 00:20:47,340
Kaio?

455
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:48,620
So, um,

456
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:49,980
see you tomorrow?

457
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:52,760
She didn't have gloves either,

458
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:53,420
did she?

459
00:20:57,420 --> 00:20:58,520
Eighteen years ago,

460
00:20:58,780 --> 00:21:00,020
I saw Kaio here,

461
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:00,820
alone,

462
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:02,440
and then she disappeared.

463
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:04,820
If I remember right,

464
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,080
they found her body

465
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:07,220
after the snow melted.

466
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:09,940
This time,

467
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:11,380
I won't leave her

468
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:12,680
standing here all alone.

469
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,340
This time?

470
00:21:17,060 --> 00:21:18,760
I'm going to save her.

471
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:28,800
I won't leave her.

472
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:31,340
cou comprend

473
00:21:31,340 --> 00:21:32,760
yes

474
00:21:32,760 --> 00:21:37,340
yeah

475
00:21:37,340 --> 00:21:40,720
yeah

476
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:44,280
osób

477
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:46,240
yeah

478
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:52,460
yeah

479
00:21:52,460 --> 00:21:55,040
yeah

480
00:21:55,040 --> 00:22:00,940
I've been with you in ahead of me

481
00:22:00,940 --> 00:22:02,940
I moved your everything

482
00:22:02,940 --> 00:22:04,840
Let me keep watching

483
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:07,440
The light piace from looks maybe

484
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:10,320
I'm waiting in space

485
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:12,360
My eyes are being put in a hand

486
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:15,220
The earth is affected by two people

487
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:17,720
In the town we didn't know

488
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:18,960
A gleaming hour

489
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:23,100
I began to see in the sky

490
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:46,100
君は僕の胸に刻まれた一番深い傷跡のようで 君が笑うこの世界の歌 取り戻すよ

